From: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 21:16:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libcxx/condition_variable: fix EINVAL abort when system clock
 not synced

When system_clock is not yet synchronized (e.g. device cold boot),
condition_variable::wait_for() may compute a negative time_point.
This causes NuttX pthread_cond_timedwait() to return EINVAL, and
libc++ treats any error other than ETIMEDOUT as fatal, calling
abort() and crashing the system.

Fix by clamping the duration to zero when negative, right after
the upper-bound check.

Signed-off-by: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
---
 src/condition_variable.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/condition_variable.cpp b/src/condition_variable.cpp
index a87399d1b7..6bbc906ece 100644
--- a/src/condition_variable.cpp
+++ b/src/condition_variable.cpp
@@ -46,6 +46,8 @@ void condition_variable::__do_timed_wait(unique_lock<mutex>& lk,
   nanoseconds d = tp.time_since_epoch();
   if (d > nanoseconds(0x59682F000000E941))
     d = nanoseconds(0x59682F000000E941);
+  else if (d < nanoseconds(0))
+    d = nanoseconds(0);
   __libcpp_timespec_t ts;
   seconds s = duration_cast<seconds>(d);
   typedef decltype(ts.tv_sec) ts_sec;
